erence-completeness":{"cache_read_tokens":15613.0,"cache_write_tokens":5857.0,"input_tokens":21476.0,"llm_calls":1,"output_tokens":1062.0,"requests":3}}}},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate the light-tier bug arm in workflow_ops.plan_review_precheck (lines 127-139, the `det_blocking: []` early return) as a required edit site and specify how an oversize description forces a BLOCK there without downgrading, since that path never reaches the existing DET short-circuit.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["workflow_ops.py:127-139: `if pctx.ticket_type == \"bug\" and not escalated_bug:` returns `{**base, \"det_blocking\": [], ... }` BEFORE the DET short-circuit","workflow_ops.py:134 comment: 'a bug is never blocked (light advisory tier)'","workflow_ops.py:162 `if det_blocks:` — the reusable short-circuit is only reached on the non-light arm (non-bug or escalated_bug)","orchestrator.py:191-211 bug_blast_radius_escalates: a bug escalates ONLY when file_impact declares a non-test path; an oversized bug with empty/test-only file_impact stays in the light tier and cannot block","registry.py:205-212 BUG_TIER_CRITERIA — the light tier is 'never blocking a bug'"],"finding":"The plan relies on reusing 'the existing deterministic plan-review short circuit' to make an oversized bug BLOCK (AC-4), but that short-circuit is unreachable for a non-escalated bug: workflow_ops.plan_review_precheck routes a bug with empty/test-only file_impact through a separate light-tier arm that sets det_blocking=[] and returns before the DET short-circuit runs — the plan does not enumerate this arm as a required edit site.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5a1224e33bce5c44","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan bullet 3 ('Preserve the description block for every work-ticket type, including the light bug-review tier...reuse the existing deterministic plan-review short circuit') and AC-4","norm_id":"na4c6800fcc91abd5","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","scenarios":["An oversized bug ticket (>8,000 chars) with empty or tests-only file_impact is submitted to plan review; the size finding is downgraded to advisory and the ticket PASSes rather than BLOCKing"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In workflow_ops.plan_review_precheck, before the light-tier bug early return, detect an oversize (blocking) p4 result and either route the ticket through the blocking-capable arm or carry the oversize finding into det_blocking for bugs specifically, so the size block survives the light-tier downgrade.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify the bug-tier carve-out: route an oversize (over-maximum) P4 description finding to `det_blocking` (or otherwise force BLOCK) on the light bug-review arm (workflow_ops.py:127-139) so the DET short-circuit is reached, since the existing short-circuit alone cannot block a non-escalated bug.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'reuse the existing deterministic plan-review short circuit so an oversize ticket returns BLOCK with coverage.llm_ran=false'","Plan: 'Preserve the description block for every work-ticket type, including the light bug-review tier'","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py:127-139 — for a non-escalated bug the arm returns early with `\"det_blocking\": []` and comment 'a bug is never blocked (light advisory tier)', folding det_blocks into det_advisory","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/workflow_ops.py:162 — the `if det_blocks:` short-circuit (the reused mechanism) is only reached on the fall-through path, never for a light-tier bug","src/rebar/llm/plan_review/det_floor.py:371-403 — p4_oversize currently returns a non-blocking DetResult; even after making the description signal blocking, that block is discarded by the bug arm's det_blocking=[]"],"finding":"The plan's stated mechanism — 'reuse the existing deterministic plan-review short circuit so an oversize ticket returns BLOCK' — cannot block a light-tier (non-escalated) bug ticket, contradicting the plan's own requirement that 'light bug review does not downgrade this size block'. The light bug arm returns before the short-circuit and downgrades every DET blocking finding to advisory.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6c5977a15055453e","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan §Plan bullets 3 & 5; AC 'The blocking plan-review behavior applies to bug, story, task, and epic tickets; light bug review does not downgrade this size block.'","norm_id":"n0d4ac271aa410c7b","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","scenarios":["A bug ticket with no non-test file_impact (not blast-radius escalated) and an 8,500-char description takes the light-tier arm; its now-blocking p4_oversize finding is downgraded to advisory and the ticket PASSes plan review instead of returning BLOCK."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"In the light bug-review arm (workflow_ops.py ~127-139), promote the oversize-description finding out of the advisory downgrade — e.g. compute an over-maximum flag and, when set, keep that single DET finding in det_blocking so the review short-circuits to BLOCK; leave AC-count/file-impact signals advisory. Then have the plan name this bug-arm change explicitly rather than relying on 'reuse the existing short circuit'.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"block","drop_reason":null,"evidence":[],"finding":"The plan asserts the existing deterministic plan-review short circuit can be reused so an oversized light-tier bug returns BLOCK, but the light-tier bug code path downgrades every DET finding (including p4_oversize) to advisory and never reaches the short circuit — so the asserted reuse mechanism cannot block a bug as-is.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f1ce3003b8cd824bb","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan §Plan bullets 3 & 4; AC 'The blocki